// Binary operators. Three questions, in this order: does it short-circuit,
// is it a comparison, is a pointer involved -- and only then which arithmetic.

// `&&`, `||` and the comma operator are not expressions in this lowering.
// The first two must not evaluate their right-hand side when the left one
// decides the answer, and an `id` expression cannot express that; they become
// two basic blocks and a frame temporary, which is emit/cfg/'s job. `,` is a
// sequence point, which is the same problem. Emitting an undefined name means
// a project that reaches one fails to build rather than running a program
// whose side effects happen in the wrong order.
bin_txt(int id) {
  string s = "NEEDS_CFG_SHORTCIRCUIT";
  if(s_of(id) != "&&" && s_of(id) != "||" && s_of(id) != ",") {
    s = bin1(id);
  }
} return string s;
given txt_fixture given pend_setup (0):("t0") then calls bin1:(0)
given txt_fixture given pend_setup (5):("t0") then calls bin1:(5)

bin1(int id) {
  string s = "";
  if(is_cmp(id) == 1) {
    s = cmp_txt(id);
  } else {
    s = bin2(id);
  }
} return string s;
given txt_fixture given pend_setup (0):("t0") then calls bin2:(0)
given txt_fixture given pend_setup (5):("t0") then calls bin2:(5)

// Either operand being an address makes this pointer arithmetic, where the
// integer side is scaled by the pointee's size. Testing both sides catches
// `n + p` as well as `p + n`, which C allows.
bin2(int id) {
  string s = "";
  if(is_ptr_either(id) == 1) {
    s = ptr_bin(id);
  } else {
    s = bin3(id);
  }
} return string s;
given txt_fixture given pend_setup (0):("t0") then calls bin3:(0)
given txt_fixture given pend_setup (5):("t0") then calls bin3:(5)
